       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 10,000 mg three times daily is 30 g/day, far above the maximum adult acetaminophen dose of 4 g/day (often limited to 3 g/day in practice). A single 10 g dose could cause serious liver toxicity, even in a patient with normal liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **1,000 mg by mouth three times daily** (3 g/day), a common regimen\n- **650 mg by mouth every 6 hours**, which is 4 times daily (2.6 g/day)\n- **500 mg by mouth every 6 hours**, which is 4 times daily (2 g/day)\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it. Please also confirm the intended dose with your supervising resident or attending."
